Title:          hwdetect.tcz
Description:    TESTING hardware detect → driver/firmware .tcz loader
Version:        0.1.0
Author:         Zendrael
Original-site:  https://forum.tinycorelinux.net/index.php?topic=27640.0
Copying-policy: GPL-2.0
Size:           8K
Extension_by:   Zendrael
Tags:           hardware drivers firmware wifi alsa detect tinycore x86
Comments:       shell scripts + curated map (no compiled code)
                ----------
                Detects PCI/USB IDs via sysfs (no lspci/lsusb) and
                selects matching firmware / wireless / alsa / bluetooth
                extensions for Tiny Core 17.x. Local-first: loads from
                tce/optional when present; optional online fetch.
                ----------
                Requires: Core (x86). Also packaged for CorePure64 (x86_64).
                Zero .dep — peer driver packages loaded dynamically.
                ----------
                Install:
                $ tce-load -i hwdetect.tcz
                Put hwdetect.tcz early on onboot.lst for portable USB.
                ----------
                After boot / CLI:
                $ hwdetect              # list suggested .tcz
                $ hwdetect --load       # load matches already in tce/optional
                $ hwdetect --fetch      # also download if network is up
                $ hwdetect --boot       # load + write tce/hwdetect.lst
                $ hwdetect --fetch --boot
                Status in the list: local | loaded | absent
                ----------
                One-shot via init.d:
                $ sudo /usr/local/etc/init.d/hwdetect start
                ----------
                Persistence:
                tce-load -i/-wi (used by --load/--fetch) appends packages
                to onboot.lst, so a fixed HDD install usually needs only
                one successful --fetch/--boot; drivers load next boot
                without calling hwdetect again.
                --boot also writes tce/hwdetect.lst (use boot code
                lst=hwdetect.lst if you want that list instead).
                Portable USB: keep hwdetect.tcz on onboot.lst to
                re-detect each boot.
                ----------
                Disable auto-run on load:
                $ sudo touch /etc/sysconfig/hwdetect.disable
                Enable online fetch during --boot / tce.installed:
                $ sudo touch /etc/sysconfig/hwdetect.fetch
                ----------
                Portable USB tip: copy common firmware-*.tcz, wifi.tcz,
                alsa.tcz into tce/optional so detection works offline.
                ----------
                Scope: drivers/firmware/wifi/alsa/bluez only — does not
                pull Xorg or window managers.
                ----------
                This extension contains:
                hwdetect-0.1.0 - GPL-2.0 -
                curated map under /usr/local/share/hwdetect/map.conf
                ----------
